WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.962
DS-1000 makes three contributions.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:08.004
First, it provides a thousand realistic problems
with diverse contexts,

00:00:08.084 --> 00:00:12.046
adapted from naturally occurring StackOverflow
questions across seven popular Python libraries.

00:00:12.126 --> 00:00:16.088
Second,

00:00:16.168 --> 00:00:20.130
it implements reliable multi-criteria evaluation
that runs test cases and checks surface-form constraints,

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.172
so accepted solutions are almost always genuinely correct.

00:00:24.252 --> 00:00:28.214
Third,

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:32.256
it proactively defends against memorization by
perturbing problems so models cannot simply

00:00:32.336 --> 00:00:36.298
recall pre-training answers.

00:00:36.378 --> 00:00:40.340
The authors release the benchmark and use it to
evaluate five state-of-the-art code models.
